CORE dfcc-only
main.c
--dfcc main --enforce-contract function/contract
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[(function\.)?precondition_instance\.1\] .*static array parameter x must provide access to its declared minimum: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^\[main\.precondition_instance\.
^\[(function\.)?precondition_instance\.2\]
^warning: ignoring
--
The harness passes an uninitialized pointer to the marked contract-checking
wrapper, so no static-array precondition is checked at that call. The single
check is at the call to the wrapped implementation, after the separately named
contract's requires clauses have been assumed, and it holds.
